' 4+1 process view - Page of a guarded area, rendered on the server (US03) · /manage as an example
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: The owner and admin areas are guarded on the server, inside Suspense (ADR 0001).
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes; refusals that do not change the sequence (they are in the text of process.md).
@startuml process-guard
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - page of a guarded area, rendered on the server (US03): /manage as an example
autonumber

participant "Browser" as C_BROWSER
box "Next.js"
  participant "proxy.ts" as WEB_PROXY
  participant "app/manage/layout.tsx" as WEB_AREA_MANAGE
  participant "AreaGuard" as WEB_GUARDS
  participant "lib/server/session.ts" as WEB_SERVER
end box
box "ASP.NET Core API"
  participant "JwtBearer" as CC_COOKIES
  participant "AuthController.Me" as API_AUTH
end box

C_BROWSER -> WEB_PROXY : GET /manage/clubs/{id}?… (with the cookies; refresh_token is not\nsent, it is Path=/api/auth) [HTTP]
WEB_PROXY -> WEB_PROXY : x-pathname = path + query (over whatever the client sent)
WEB_PROXY -> WEB_AREA_MANAGE : NextResponse.next with the header
WEB_AREA_MANAGE --> C_BROWSER : 200: the static shell starts streaming (the Suspense fallback\nis null)
WEB_AREA_MANAGE -> WEB_GUARDS : AreaGuard profile=Owner (inside Suspense, because it reads cookies)
WEB_GUARDS -> WEB_SERVER : getSessionAccount()
alt no cookies
  WEB_SERVER --> WEB_GUARDS : null, without calling the API
else
  WEB_SERVER -> CC_COOKIES : GET {API_INTERNAL_URL}/api/auth/me with the user's Cookie,\nno-store cache [HTTP]
  CC_COOKIES -> API_AUTH : Valid token (no database) → Me
  API_AUTH --> WEB_SERVER : 200 account, or 401 (no session or expired token)
  WEB_SERVER --> WEB_GUARDS : account or null; any other status throws → the area's error.tsx
end
WEB_GUARDS -> WEB_GUARDS : headers().get('x-pathname'); areaDecision('Owner', account,\nrequestedPath)
alt no session
  WEB_GUARDS -> WEB_GUARDS : redirect(loginUrl(safeNext(requestedPath, 'Owner')))
  WEB_GUARDS --> C_BROWSER : The 200 status has already gone out: Next.js streams a meta tag\nhttp-equiv=refresh to /login?next=…
  C_BROWSER -> C_BROWSER : Goes to /login: GuestOnly and silent refresh (browser refresh\ndiagram)
else another profile
  WEB_GUARDS -> WEB_GUARDS : redirect(profileHome(profile)): '/' or '/admin', also by meta
else owner
  WEB_GUARDS --> C_BROWSER : Streams AreaHeader and the page in place of the fallback
end
@enduml
